---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy | plansplease"
  description="How local and cloud HTML pages are handled in the plansplease alpha."
  activePath="privacy"
>
  <section class="prose-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Private by default.</h1>
    <p>
      plansplease is still in alpha. This page describes how the current local and cloud workflows
      handle the HTML pages you give them.
    </p>

    <ul class="prose-list">
      <li>
        <h2>Cloud pages belong to your account</h2>
        <p>
          Files uploaded to the cloud workspace are associated with the signed-in account. The
          dashboard only lists that account's documents.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Cloud previews require your session</h2>
        <p>
          In the current alpha, preview requests check the authenticated session before returning
          the stored HTML. There is no public sharing link yet.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Local pages stay on your machine</h2>
        <p>
          The CLI binds its local daemon to the loopback interface. A local snapshot is served by
          the machine where you ran the command.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Uploads start with standalone HTML</h2>
        <p>
          The cloud upload flow currently accepts one standalone HTML file at a time. Bundled
          assets and page folders will come later with object storage support.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="page-note">This summary will be replaced with full product terms before a public launch.</p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
